Player download
---------------
Duvy does not bundle mpv in its installers. On first launch the app downloads a Windows
build of mpv into its app data directory, verifying every file against the release's
`sha256.txt` before use. The `player-1` release of this repository serves two files:

- `mpv.exe`, a Windows build of mpv reporting version `v0.41.0-1227-ge471496c5`. mpv is free
  software distributed under GPL-2.0-or-later. The corresponding source is published by the mpv
  project at https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv; the commit named in the version string is in that
  repository. The build also uses FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), libplacebo
  (https://github.com/haasn/libplacebo) and other libraries, each under its own license and with
  its own published source. This repository does not ship a copy of mpv's license text; the
  upstream terms are in the mpv repository's `Copyright` and `LICENSE.GPL` files.
- `d3dcompiler_43.dll`, Microsoft's Direct3D 43 shader compiler redistributable, included
  alongside the mpv Windows build. It is Microsoft software governed by Microsoft's
  redistributable terms, not by the GPL.

A user-supplied mpv set in Settings is used instead when present and is governed by that copy's
own license. Because the player is fetched at runtime, an installer built from this repository
does not redistribute mpv. Anyone redistributing the player files themselves should keep this
NOTICE and keep the corresponding source locations available.

Content and services
--------------------
Duvy ships no media, no catalogs, no addons and no scrapers. All metadata, catalogs and
streams come from third-party addon URLs that the user installs, from media servers the user
connects, or from files the user opens. TMDB data is used only when the user supplies a key.
Users are responsible for the addons and services they configure and for complying with the laws
and terms that apply to them. P2P playback exposes the user's IP address to other peers. Debrid
resolution uses the user's own account and remains subject to that provider's terms.

Addon protocol
--------------
The addon transport implemented here follows the publicly documented Stremio addon protocol.
Stremio is a trademark of its respective owner; this project is not affiliated with Stremio.

Third-party services
--------------------
- TMDB: this product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.
- Trakt: the user creates their own Trakt API application. Duvy is not affiliated with
  Trakt.
- Nuvio Cloud sync: an unofficial client for the backend used by the official Nuvio apps. It may
  change or stop working without notice. Duvy is not affiliated with Nuvio Media.
- Stremio account sync: an unofficial client for the same `api.strem.io` endpoints the official
  Stremio apps use. It may change or stop working without notice. Duvy is not affiliated
  with Stremio.
- IntroDB: community intro and outro timestamps, queried by IMDb id. Duvy is not
  affiliated with IntroDB.
- Jellyfin and Emby: the user connects their own server. Duvy is not affiliated with either
  project.
- Debrid: the user connects their own account. Duvy is not affiliated with any provider.
- mpv: playback is performed by the downloaded or user-installed mpv, under the terms described
  above.

Third-party crates and npm packages are used under their own licenses; see `Cargo.lock` and
`bun.lock` for the exact set. Duvy's own source is MIT-licensed; see `LICENSE`.
